Raven archive 18 -- route 516.
A maester recorded signs of Winter beyond the ridge.
Heavy clouds were taken as a sign of Winter.
Villagers stored grain after the first hint of winter.
The river has begun to freeze as Winter approaches.
A child drew the shape of a DRAGON on the wall.
A second copy of the message was sent by sea.
The council discussed how long Winter might last.
The maester collected reports concerning a dragon.
The map was copied and placed inside a sealed chest.
A distant roar convinced the riders that a dragon was near.
A small patrol was sent toward Tyrion.
Supplies arrived without any missing crates.
A second messenger confirmed the report at sunset.
